{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5471) from a code generation pipeline. The task is to implement srd071 requirements R2.1 through R2.4 in `cmd/numfmt`, which adds format control features to the numfmt utility. Specifically:\n   - R2.1: `--format=FORMAT` - printf-style format string for output (width, precision, left-alignment)\n   - R2.2: `--padding=N` - pad output to N characters (positive=right-align, negative=left-align)\n   - R2.3: `--round=METHOD` - rounding control (up/ceiling, down/floor, from-zero, towards-zero, nearest)\n   - R2.4: `--suffix=SUFFIX` - append suffix after numeric value and unit suffix\n   \n   Each feature must have at least one differential test case comparing against `gnumfmt`. The code must compile, pass `go vet`, and tests must pass (or skip gracefully if gnumfmt is not installed).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary vs GNU reference binary (`gnumfmt`)\n   - Go `flag` package for CLI argument parsing\n   - Printf-style format string parsing for `--format`\n   - Number formatting with SI/IEC suffixes (1000-based vs 1024-based)\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `pkg/sys`\n   - Execution constitution mandates: 40-line function limit, copyright headers, no git commands, no scope creep\n   - stderr normalization in tests (replacing \"gnumfmt:\" with \"numfmt:\")\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd071-numfmt.yaml`\n     - Source of truth for all requirements. R2.1-R2.4 define format control features.\n     - R2.1: `--format=FORMAT` with printf-style width, precision, left-alignment\n     - R2.2: `--padding=N` with positive=right-align, negative=left-align\n     - R2.3: `--round=METHOD` with values: up, down, from-zero, towards-zero, nearest\n     - R2.4: `--suffix=SUFFIX` appended after numeric value and unit suffix\n     - Non-goals: no locale-aware digit grouping, no --grouping\n\n   - `cmd/numfmt/main.go` (278 lines, existing implementation of R1.1-R1.4)\n     - Currently has: `--to` and `--from` flags, `isValidUnit()`, `processLine()`, `processToken()`, `splitWhitespace()`, `parseNumber()`, `hasSuffix()`, `extractSuffix()`, `formatNumber()`, `formatRaw()`, `formatWithSuffix()`, `suffixesForUnit()`, `suffixMultipliers()`, `baseForUnit()`, `endsWithLetter()`\n     - Key function signatures:\n       - `func processLine(line, fromUnit, toUnit string) error`\n       - `func processToken(token, fromUnit, toUnit string) error`\n       - `func formatNumber(val float64, unit string) string`\n       - `func formatWithSuffix(val, base float64, suffixes []string) string`\n     - Uses `flag` package, `bufio.Scanner` for stdin\n     - Rounding is currently hardcoded to `math.Ceil` in `formatWithSuffix`\n\n   - `cmd/numfmt/numfmt_test.go` (177 lines, existing differential tests)\n     - Has `stderrNorm` normalizer: `bytes.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\"gnumfmt:\"), []byte(\"numfmt:\"))`\n     - `TestDiff` builds binary, looks up `gnumfmt`, runs 28 test cases\n     - Test cases cover: to_si, to_iec, to_iec_i, from_si, from_iec, passthrough, multiline, operands, errors\n     - Pattern: `testutils.DiffTest{Name, Args, Stdin, ExitCode, Normalize}`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. The task was just beginning (files were read, implementation not started).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD and existing code to understand the current state. The existing implementation only handles R1.1-R1.4 (basic --to/--from conversion, stdin/operand input). The R2 features (format, padding, round, suffix) need to be added by:\n     - Adding new flag definitions in `main()`\n     - Modifying `processLine()` and `pro